# The build context is the REPO ROOT (see bb.edn's docker task), while the
# Dockerfile copies a single jar out of target/. Without this file every
# `docker build` would upload node_modules, the Maven cache and the whole jj
# store to the daemon before ignoring all of it.
#
# Note the deliberate asymmetry: target/ is NOT ignored, because the jar is the
# one thing the image actually needs.

.git/
.jj/
.cpcache/
.shadow-cljs/
.lsp/
.clj-kondo/
node_modules/

# Game data never belongs in an image. A stray local SQLite file baked into a
# layer would ship somebody's half-finished game to the server — and, worse,
# would be shadowed by the /data volume at runtime, so it would sit there
# invisible and confusing rather than being obviously wrong.
data/
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal

# Sources are not needed: the jar contains them. Keeping them out means editing
# a .cljc file cannot invalidate the image layer cache.
src/
test/
dev/
build/
resources/

.env
deploy/.env
*.md
.DS_Store
.nrepl-port
